nodes.body:
@DarkSharpness, replying to [your review](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37625#pullrequestreview-5325032535):

> The legacy topk part LGTM.

The v2 changes, including the coarse-bound and all-equal paths, are removed from this PR. The diff now covers the four legacy/v1 selectors so those fixes can be reviewed and merged independently. I will submit the v2 changes in a separate PR.

@zRzRzRzRzRzRzR, replying to [your selector-scope comment](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37625#issuecomment-5523433093):

> There are several other copies of the same code affect all dsa model.

The patch covers all four legacy/v1 copies: KPool JIT, DeepSeek-V4 JIT v1, legacy CUDA AOT and DeepSeek-V4 AOT. The separate QSA fast_topk copy on newer main is outside this patch.

@DarkSharpness, replying to [your rebase request](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37625#issuecomment-5844258424):

> @ormandj could you please rebase to the latest main branch?

Rebased onto main `c7be3e935b5`.

@AranKomat, replying to [your AMD test-coverage question](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/37625#issuecomment-5649576935):

> Are there particular AMD boundary/graph cases you would like added to the existing regression suite?

The suite compares selected-value multisets and allows index swaps among equal scores. It includes oversized and exact-capacity bins, ties, offsets and changed inputs. The retained ROCm AOT cases have not been rerun on gfx942; the current GPU results are from SM120.

